{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/117764-compact-conspiracy-idea-the-destroyers-of-living-idols","id":117764,"title":"Compact/Conspiracy Idea: The Destroyers of Living Idols","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-22T18:16:36-07:00","id":117764,"title":"Compact/Conspiracy Idea: The Destroyers of Living Idols","content":"Anyway, back on the old forums, a certain idiot whose name will not be mentioned here on the basis that without it, he may not be able to realize the forums moved and so come to bother us again came up with the idea of god hunters.<br /> <br /> Sadly, he mainly used this as yet another pulpit to whine about Christian influences, at all, in the nWoD (seriously, he was pissed off because Demons is about playing Fallen Angels, never mind the fact that it's spelled out right there the God-Machine is not any YHVH anyone would recognize), it was a good idea, at least.<br /> <br /> I can imagine that a lot of people get pissed at WoD cults to begin with, and discovering that many of them worship physically existent supernatural beings who are almost invariably egomaniacs on a power trip (like mortal cult leaders) would probably result in at least a few of them banding together. Cue Vigil.<br /> <br /> All we need is an ideology, volia - instant Compact and/or Conspiracy.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking something like a group of Freemasons who view supernaturals proclaiming themselves gods infringing upon the design of the Great Architect of the Universe (ie, a God of your choosing, they don't officially judge if it's the Judeo-Islamic-Christian one, Brahma, or the Flying Spaghetti Monster in your view), causing great ruination as the structure of reality has flaws introduced. They don't mind working with most supernaturals to bust cults if they do not &quot;infringe on the design&quot;, ie form cults around themselves, one of their advantages (and satirizing the tendency of paranoids to keep ascribing sinister motives to a glorified clubhouse - they work with monsters, but only to free the world from those who act like monsters, ie not very monstrous monsters).<br /> <br /> <b>Any other ideas?</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T18:32:40-07:00","id":117767,"title":"","content":"I like it. Reminds me of the Lodge of the Fallen Idol, faith-killers. They actually have a faith-detection fetish. The Lancea Sanctum also has a Godslayers faction who slay followers of false gods.<br /> <br /> That said, would this be more appropriate as a faction of an already existing compact or conspiracy, such as the Long Night or Malleus Maleficarum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-22-2014, 11:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T19:35:35-07:00","id":117799,"title":"","content":"Would not be surprising. Really, this is also a place to put Freemasons in, because they're such an interesting group in urban fantasy, even if they come off as more secretive than they really are (I think they've made videos of their induction and promotion ceremonies, too). I can imagine them being pissed at cults in general too, since Masonry superficially resembles one - enough to be upset by the comparisons (they're more like a mortal Consilium than anything). Also a good place for a splinter of the larger group to quietly voice their concerns about something very scary and very vicious overtaking their community, one that doesn't like being criticized (as do most Hunter compacts, but I imagine the quiet dissent came before the Vigil in this case).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T10:15:35-07:00","id":117974,"title":"","content":"Actually that gives me an idea if these guys are a Conspiracy; Social-focused Endowment, essentially convincing reality to help them through philosophical argument.<br /> <br /> How that would work is beyond me, but it sounds like a spectacular concept that relates to the &quot;seeking truth&quot; aspects of a splinter lodge of Masons, and relates to their ethos (showing that the supernatural &quot;gods&quot; the cults they target worship have very little wisdom about reality, hence why they're damaging the world through their reckless egomania. Please ignore the fact that convincing reality of your ideals <i>is </i>essentially what the Endowment is doing, though they think they're simply doing it wisely, intentionally, and with the cosmos' explicit permission given how using that Endowment is a matter of winning it over briefly, ergo not actually damaging reality that much).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T10:23:30-07:00","id":117982,"title":"","content":"Actually, an old idea of mine is called Nimrod's Children- a group of hunters who believe that humanity should be free from the influence of all gods and all religions, in order to create their own destiny. They name themselves after Nimrod, the first name to rebel against God, although most of them don't really believe in the bible. Actually, their official claim is that there are no gods, and that the &quot;gods&quot; are simply powerful beings who took the mantle of a divine being in order to manipulate humanity. Some of them recognize that there are some weird, higher powers (like the God Machine, or the Exrachs or even the Wyrd or the Principle), and they work in order to find a way to break their hold upon humanity's fate. I've thought about them at a Conspiracy scale, with an Endowment which manipulate the hidden, small angels which are hidden through the world, but I assume they could work on a lesser scale, with maybe an &quot;half an endowment&quot; or just a Compact Endowment.<br /> <br /> At least, that's what I have in mind right now :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T12:18:13-07:00","id":118046,"title":"","content":"I find the idea of humans standing up form themselves against Gods, while awesome, to be a trite obvious. Therefore I greatly amused myself by coming up with the exact opposite.<br /> <br /> High priest - &quot;behold an irrefutable proof that my God exists. Use your knowladge to build weapons for His armies and you shall be granted wealth beyond imagining.&quot;<br /> Null Mysteriis 1 - &quot;Looks like Gods exist, I guess we're a weapons lab now.&quot;<br /> Null Mysteriis 2 - &quot;Hold on a second, if I wanted to be rich I wouldn't have studied quantum physics and this God sounds like a douche. If one God exists maybe others, Ganesha is a god of both wisdom and compassion.&quot;<br /> Null Mysteriis 3 - &quot;But reincarnation? I like the idea of eternal paradise.&quot;<br /> Null Mysteriis 4 - &quot;So we want a God with agreeable morals, who values the mind and offers an awesome afterlife. And they have to exist, lets go to the library and look up some likely candidates!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T07:50:21-07:00","id":118428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually that gives me an idea if these guys are a Conspiracy; Social-focused Endowment, essentially convincing reality to help them through philosophical argument. </div> </div> </div>So, while changelings bargain with reality, Masons must convince the universe that they are right. I love it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T11:03:11-07:00","id":118504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/117764-compact-conspiracy-idea-the-destroyers-of-living-idols#post117764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking something like a group of Freemasons who view supernaturals proclaiming themselves gods infringing upon the design of the Great Architect of the Universe (ie, a God of your choosing, they don't officially judge if it's the Judeo-Islamic-Christian one, Brahma, or the Flying Spaghetti Monster in your view), causing great ruination as the structure of reality has flaws introduced.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd suggest making them a bit more specific in what they believe, not least because not every god is a logical candidate for that sort of great architect (for example, Brahma belongs to a religion that claims countless gods). More positively, I'd suggest making them explicitly Deist - it at least nods towards what you said of not nominating a particular god (though some Deists did consider themselves Christian as well), it has historical associations with Freemasons, and values rationality, which fits in with your argument-based endowment idea - also, they detested superstition and &quot;priestcraft,&quot; both of which would exemplified by supernaturals playing god.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T11:45:12-07:00","id":118522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/117764-compact-conspiracy-idea-the-destroyers-of-living-idols?p=118428#post118428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, while changelings bargain with reality, Masons must convince the universe that they are right. I love it!</div> </div> </div> </div>You should have a look at Talecrafting and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/475-wyrd-sorcery\">Wyrd Sorcery</a> then; both of them are variants on tricking the universe into doing what you want, so maybe an antithesis will do for the Endowment.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}